{
  "dom_id": "step-q159934",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{7}$ is an I.I.D random sample with ${X}_{i}∼\\text{Exp}(\\theta )$ and unknown rate parameter $\\theta .$ For a particular sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{7},$ you're given that \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}=38.9.\n$$\n\nGiven that the log-likelihood function of the sample is\n\n$$\nl(\\theta )=a\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +b\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$\n\n*Hint: The probability density function for an exponential random variable is given by* \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\theta {e}^{-\\theta x},\\,x\\ge 0.\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that if ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ are independent and identically distributed continuous random variables with probability density function $f(x;\\theta ),$ where $\\theta $ is an unknown parameter, then the log-likelihood function of a random sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}l(\\theta ) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡L(\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({\\prod }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i};\\theta )) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(f({x}_{i};\\theta )).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we are given a sample of $n=7$ independent exponential random variables with unknown parameter $\\theta ,$ for which the probability density function is\n\n$$\nf(x,\\theta )=\\theta {e}^{-\\theta x},\\,x\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nNext, we write down the log-density function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡f(x,\\theta ) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\theta {e}^{-\\theta x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-\\theta x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -\\theta x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can calculate the log-likelihood function as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}l(\\theta ) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -\\theta {x}_{i}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -\\theta {\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =n\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -\\theta {\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are told that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}=38.9$ and $n=7.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}l(\\theta ) & =7\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta -\\theta \\cdot 38.9 \\\\  & =7\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\theta +(-38.9)\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=7+(-38.9)=-31.9.\n$$",
